// Vault integration reads/writes custom_metadata (chronowarden_ttl, chronowarden_severity, chronowarden_owner)
// and discovers KV v2 secret engines for monitoring
// Authentication supports token-based (token, token_env, token_file) and AppRole (role_id, secret_id) methods
// Config is the source of truth - severity cascade: secret config → engine config → vault severity → global default
// Owner profiles support notification routing via email and webhook channels
// Secrets API reads from the database cache populated by sync, not from an in-memory store
// severity: none means monitor but never alert/rotate (replaces chronowarden_enabled field)